# text
seg-c55e49fd2a72 = Kshana for JetBrains IDEs

# text
# c1: .toml
seg-c1a917b85688 = Kshana for JetBrains IDEs runs the Kshana PNT-resilience simulator from inside any JetBrains IDE (IntelliJ IDEA, CLion, RustRover, PyCharm and the others). Right-click a scenario <c1/>, choose <b>Run Kshana Scenario</b>, and the figures of merit and the result JSON appear in the Kshana tool window.

# text
seg-f044930f2fc9 = Install it from the JetBrains Marketplace: <a1>Kshana — PNT simulator</a1>, or in any JetBrains IDE open <b>Settings → Plugins → Marketplace</b> and search for "Kshana".

# attr:title
seg-34bdcfd66ded = In the repository branch these docs come from; not yet on GitHub

# text
# c1: kshana
# c2: cargo install kshana
# c3: PATH
seg-ad19b68b2e25 = The plugin runs your installed <c1/> command. Install it with <c2/> (see <s1>Developers</s1>) and, if it is not on your <c3/>, point the plugin at it in <b>Settings → Tools → Kshana</b>. The plugin loads in every JetBrains IDE from { "2024.3" } on.

# text
# c1: .toml
seg-e1c3eff8429c = <b>Run Kshana Scenario</b> on any scenario <c1/>, from the editor or the project view, with the output in the Kshana tool window.

# text
seg-c4904a0bfb76 = <b>Validate Scenario</b>, <b>List Scenario Kinds</b> and <b>Insert Example Scenario</b>: check a file, see every kind, and start from any bundled scenario without overwriting a file.

# text
seg-4b4d21df50d0 = <b>Assess Receiver Trust</b> and <b>Assess Receiver Stream</b>: the trust timeline of a receiver-trust scenario or a stored NMEA log, with a { "0" }–{ "100" } score and its reasons. Advisory software, not type-approved navigation equipment: the operator remains responsible for the navigation of the vessel.

# text
seg-ff8252ad4fc6 = <b>Export Scenario</b> (SP3, OMM, OEM, CZML, KML, GeoJSON, STK and SigMF; simulated output only), <b>Animate Scenario</b> and <b>Import Route</b>.

# text
seg-096ea53c3eb4 = <b>Generate Training NMEA</b> and <b>Export Test-Bench Files</b> for training and for a laboratory GNSS simulator. They write text files only and no signal.

# text
seg-94ccbbec08bd = <b>Build Interference Map</b> and <b>Route Exposure</b> from ADS-B or AIS recordings. A degraded cell does not identify interference as the cause, and it is not a forecast.

# text
seg-c1d5e12c1d51 = <b>Build Compliance Report</b> and <b>Show Compliance Mapping</b>: the public-framework mapping, with the engine's own statement word for word. It is not a certification.

# text
seg-a2c070b52b7d = <b>Create Evidence Pack</b>, <b>Verify Evidence Pack</b> and <b>Attach Timestamp</b>: evidence packs signed with a key you already hold, and verified only against a signer you pin.

# text
seg-60a463a04505 = <b>Render Trust Telemetry</b> and <b>Fit Sensor Parameters from IMU Log</b>: Prometheus text, CEF or LEEF events and Home Assistant lines printed to the tool window, and the accelerometer and gyro parameters fitted from a stationary IMU log (MODELLED).

# text
seg-a30742f63c48 = The long-running streaming commands, the IQ commands and key generation stay on the command line, because an IDE action runs a command to completion.

# text
seg-e8844beb1351 = Licence and support

